  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "As-cast equiatomic HfMoTaTiZr has a density of approximately 10.21 g/cm³.",
      "field": "material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast equiatomic HfMoTaTiZr has a room-temperature yield strength of approximately 1600 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast equiatomic HfMoTaTiZr has a yield strength of approximately 855 MPa at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing part of Ta with Nb will reduce the density of HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "hypothesis; intervention; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb is lighter than Ta.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb and Ta are chemically and structurally similar.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb and Ta have similar atomic radii.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial Nb-for-Ta substitution will preserve comparable lattice parameters and short-range order.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial Nb-for-Ta substitution will preserve the local lattice distortion responsible for dislocation resistance.",
      "field": "structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Local lattice distortion impedes dislocation glide and provides solid-solution strengthening in this alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The as-cast alloy's high-temperature strength involves dislocation-pinning mechanisms that can largely be retained after Nb substitution.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A suitable balance of refractory elements can preserve a stable disordered BCC or otherwise relevant single-phase structure after Nb substitution.",
      "field": "mechanism; boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preserving lattice distortion and phase stability will keep room- and high-temperature yield strengths close to those of as-cast HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "hypothesis; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy may achieve a density reduction on the order of 10% relative to 10.21 g/cm³.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy is predicted to retain approximately 90–100% of the 1600 MPa room-temperature yield strength.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy is predicted to retain approximately 90–100% of the 855 MPa yield strength at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed hypothesis applies under quasi-static uniaxial compression at room temperature and 1000 °C, at approximately 1×10^-4 s^-1.",
      "field": "conditions; boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis is conditional on retaining a single-phase disordered microstructure without intermetallic formation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb substitution may alter local lattice distortion, phase stability, or solute clustering and thereby degrade mechanical performance, particularly at high temperature.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed rejection thresholds are a density reduction below approximately 10% together with room-temperature yield strength below 1440 MPa or 1000 °C yield strength below approximately 770 MPa.",
      "field": "falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
  ],
